diff --git a/crates/benilla-ui/docs/mod-api.md b/crates/benilla-ui/docs/mod-api.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..72043c79
--- /dev/null
+++ b/crates/benilla-ui/docs/mod-api.md
@@ -0,0 +1,88 @@
+# Open Mod API 0.1 (`Mod`)
+
+WrathUnleashed's own mod surface: one global table, `Mod`, on top of the stock 3.3.5a API.
+Source: `src/script/mod_api.lua` (Lua half) and `src/script/mod_api.rs` (host half). Tests:
+`src/script/tests/mod_api.rs`.
+
+Rule: everything listed here really works on this client. `Mod.Api.Has` reports a capability
+only when it is real, and a hook point exists only where something fires it.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+| Call | Answer |
+|---|---|
+| `Mod.Api.Version` | `"0.1"` |
+| `Mod.Api.Has("api:0.1")` | the API version |
+| `Mod.Api.Has("compat:<Name>")` | a backport call is defined right now (`C_NamePlate`, `UnitTokenFromGUID`, `GetSpellBaseCooldown`, `GetItemInfoInstant`, `UnitOwner`, `UnitOccupations`, `UnitIsControlled`, `UnitIsDisarmed`, `FlashWindow`, `IsWindowFocused`, `FocusWindow`, `CopyToClipboard`) |
+| `Mod.Api.Has("hook:<point>")` | the hook point exists and can attach now |
+| `Mod.Api.Has("on" \| "slash" \| "store" \| "packet" \| "hook")` | the feature |
+| `Mod.Api.HookPoints()` | the hook point names, sorted |
+| `Mod.Api.Mods()` | the `mod.toml` manifests the addon loader read: `{ addon, id, name, version, api, permissions = {...} }` |
+
+## Events, slash commands, storage
+
+- `Mod.On(event, fn) -> cancel`: `fn(...)` gets the event's arguments after every frame's
+  `OnEvent`; no frame needed. `cancel()` unregisters.
+- `Mod.Slash.Register("KEY", "/cmd" | {"/cmd", "/alias"}, fn(msg))`: a stock `SlashCmdList`
+  row (`SLASH_KEY1`, ...). A missing leading `/` is added.
+- `Mod.Store.Account(id)` / `Mod.Store.Character(id)`: a table that persists like
+  SavedVariables. Both live in one saved global, `OVMOD_STORE = { account = { [id] = {} },
+  character = { ["Realm-Name"] = { [id] = {} } } }`, registered with `RegisterForSave`, so it is
+  written at logout and run back before addons load. `Character` raises until the player exists.
+
+## Hooks: `Mod.Hook(point, fn [, "pre" | "post"]) -> cancel`
+
+| Point | Phases | `fn` gets | Fired by |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `nameplate:added` / `nameplate:removed` | pre, post | `unit, plate` | `NAME_PLATE_UNIT_ADDED` / `_REMOVED` |
+| `spellcast:start` / `spellcast:stop` / `spellcast:succeeded` | pre, post | `unit, spell, rank, ...` | `UNIT_SPELLCAST_START` / `_STOP` / `_SUCCEEDED` |
+| `combatlog` | pre, post | the event's arguments | `COMBAT_LOG_EVENT_UNFILTERED` |
+| `tooltip:unit` | post | `tooltip` | GameTooltip's `OnTooltipSetUnit` |
+| `tooltip:item` | post | `tooltip, link` | GameTooltip `SetHyperlink`, `SetBagItem`, `SetInventoryItem`, `SetLootItem`, `SetMerchantItem` |
+| `chat:filter` | pre | the stock filter's arguments; return `true` to hide | `ChatFrame_AddMessageEventFilter` on every player chat lane |
+
+`pre` runs before any frame's `OnEvent` for the event, `post` after every frame (including
+`RegisterAllEvents` frames). A pre hook observes; it cannot cancel the event. The default phase
+is `post` where a point has both. A raising hook goes to the error handler and the rest still run.
+
+Not hookable from an addon: the login screen, the character list and the loading screen run in
+the glue VM, where no addon code is loaded.
+
+## Packets: `Mod.Packet`
+
+```lua
+Mod.Packet.Register("pings")
+Mod.Packet.On("pings", "marker", function(data) ... end)   -- one handler per modId/name
+Mod.Packet.Send("pings", "ping", "1.5,2,3,0,attack")        -- returns the part count
+```
+
+Transport: addon whispers to oneself, which a server script (mod-ale `ov_modapi.lua`) answers.
+
+### Wire format
+
+- Prefix `OVMOD`, chat type WHISPER, language `LANG_ADDON`, target the player's own name.
+- One message per part: `<modId> TAB <name> TAB <i>/<n> TAB <data>`; parts are 1-based, may
+  arrive in any order; `data` is everything after the third TAB (it may hold tabs).
+- `modId` and `name`: 1-32 characters of `[A-Za-z0-9_.-]`. `data`: any bytes but NUL.
+- Client to server: the core drops a line whose `"OVMOD\t" .. text` is over 255 bytes, so each
+  part carries at most `249 - #modId - #name - #"i/n" - 3` data bytes; the client sizes parts by
+  that formula, at most 64 parts. An empty payload is one part (`pings\tmarker\t1/1\t`).
+- Server to client: parts of up to 2000 data bytes as a whisper (type 7) whose sender is the
+  player. The client accepts `OVMOD` only on the WHISPER lane from `UnitName("player")`,
+  reassembles by `modId`/`name` (a new part count restarts the buffer), and calls the handler
+  with the whole payload.
+- The send bypasses `SendAddonMessage`'s escape scan: the payload is data, not chat text.
+
+## `mod.toml`
+
+Beside an addon's `.toc`, read by the addon loader at world entry:
+
+```toml
+id = "pings"
+name = "Pings & World Markers"
+version = "1.0.0"
+api = "0.1"
+permissions = ["packet", "store"]
+```
+
+Permissions are listed by `Mod.Api.Mods()`; nothing enforces or shows them yet.
